  "first turn / native": "# Migent workflow stage

## Response contract

Start the response with a status header, then a blank line, then the report:

\`\`\`
status: complete | question | blocked
blocker: <reason>   ← only with blocked
\`\`\`

| Status | Meaning |
| :--- | :--- |
| \`complete\` | The stage's work is finished, artifact written. |
| \`question\` | You need a human answer to continue. |
| \`blocked\` | An obstacle you cannot resolve in this turn. |

## Asking questions

Write the question document to the question file (see Execution), then return \`status: question\`. Migent reads the file only for that status. Keep choices out of the report body.

\`\`\`json
{"schema_version":1,"questions":[{"question":"...","context":"...","selection":"single|multiple","recommended":["A"],"options":[{"label":"...","description":"..."}]}]}
\`\`\`

- Each question needs 2–26 options.
- Omit IDs: Migent letters options A, B, C… and numbers questions 1, 2, 3… in order.
- Optional: \`description\` on an option; \`recommended\` on a question, a list of option letters (at most one for \`single\`).
- Free-text answers are always allowed.
- Several questions per file are allowed; all must be answered before the stage continues.
- Present choices neutrally. Never decide on the human's behalf.

## Stage: make (role: worker)

### Verify

After \`status: complete\`, Migent runs these commands in order. Completion counts only if all exit 0; otherwise you get the report and fix it here.

- \`check-one\`
- \`check-two\`

## Execution

- Task: \`<SESSION>/task.md\`
- Session dir: \`<SESSION>\` (shared session files)
- Question file: \`<QFILE>\`
- Artifacts: \`<ART>\`

## Do

Read the task, then carry out the stage.
Write the artifact as \`make.md\` in the artifacts directory.",
